  "full_text": "**\n\n**Solution 2:** The bat costs $1.10 and the ball costs $0.10.\n</think>\n\nTo determine the cost of the ball, let's break down the problem step by step.\n\n**Let:**\n- **Ball Cost** = \\( b \\) dollars.\n- **Bat Cost** = \\( b + 1 \\) dollars (since the bat costs \\$1.00 more than the ball).\n\n**Given:**\n\\[\n\\text{Ball Cost} + \\text{Bat Cost} = \\$1.10\n\\]\n\\[\nb + (b + 1) = 1.10\n\\]\n\\[\n2b + 1 = 1.10\n\\]\n\\[\n2b = 1.10 - 1\n\\]\n\\[\n2b = 0.10\n\\]\n\\[\nb = \\frac{0.10}{2} = 0.05\n\\]\n\n**Conclusion:**\nThe ball costs **5 cents**.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0.05}\n\\]"
}